And they couldn't be fake looking.

778
00:29:54.520 --> 00:29:56.180
Like, they couldn't be, like, blue and pink.

779
00:29:56.500 --> 00:30:00.340
So he did eventually find them at a place called Hollywood Costumes.

780
00:30:00.560 --> 00:30:03.760
He was particularly proud of the tiny sunglasses that he found.

781
00:30:03.760 --> 00:30:06.440
This poster ends up coming back in conflict resolution.

782
00:30:06.440 --> 00:30:07.840
Like you said, it stayed up there.

783
00:30:07.980 --> 00:30:09.680
But then it comes back again.

784
00:30:09.840 --> 00:30:10.620
It comes back again.

785
00:30:10.620 --> 00:30:13.960
I would like to know the two babies that were in the poster.

786
00:30:14.180 --> 00:30:15.160
Oh, guys.

787
00:30:15.420 --> 00:30:16.380
Where are they today?

788
00:30:16.780 --> 00:30:19.640
If you are a baby in that poster.

789
00:30:19.720 --> 00:30:25.640
From the baby jazz poster, will you please write to us at officeladies at earwolf.com?

790
00:30:25.640 --> 00:30:34.680
One thing about that baby jazz poster, I remember Mike Schur telling me that they thought it was really funny that Angela would really enjoy babies dressed as adults.

791
00:30:35.040 --> 00:30:35.520
Okay.

792
00:30:35.780 --> 00:30:36.620
Where are we?

793
00:30:36.800 --> 00:30:38.760
Well, we're talking about the gifts.

794
00:30:39.140 --> 00:30:43.880
And Mike Schur actually said that the gifts were incredibly hard to manage.

795
00:30:44.280 --> 00:30:49.480
Because they start off as Secret Santa, so everybody had a person that they bought a specific gift for.

796
00:30:49.680 --> 00:30:53.800
And then you had to track the gifts as they went around in the Yankee swap.

797
00:30:53.800 --> 00:31:01.280
He actually, in the script of this episode, there is a whole page where he lists the gifts.

798
00:31:01.600 --> 00:31:03.100
Who bought who what?

799
00:31:03.320 --> 00:31:06.780
And he did this for Veda, our script supervisor.

800
00:31:07.080 --> 00:31:17.360
We haven't really talked about her, but Veda's job is to sit and watch every take that is filmed and make notes about everything that happens continuity-wise.

801
00:31:17.800 --> 00:31:19.720
So, I mean, like, really specific.

802
00:31:20.080 --> 00:31:26.560
So, like, if in a scene you take a drink of your tea on a certain line and then scratch your nose on another one,

803
00:31:26.700 --> 00:31:31.200
Veda writes it down so that you do it the same every time for editing purposes.

804
00:31:31.200 --> 00:31:38.100
Yeah, or Veda would come up to us and say, Angela, you were holding that pen in your left hand in the first take.

805
00:31:38.280 --> 00:31:41.060
And in the second take, you picked it up and held it in your right hand.

806
00:31:41.360 --> 00:31:42.740
So, that's not going to match.

807
00:31:42.860 --> 00:31:46.560
So, you need to pick which hand you're going to hold that pen in and do it in every take the same way.

808
00:31:46.740 --> 00:31:51.420
Yeah, because otherwise, when you edit it together, the pen is magically bouncing from hand to hand.

809
00:31:51.620 --> 00:31:51.940
Mm-hmm.

810
00:31:51.940 --> 00:32:00.680
So, Mike was really worried about Veda in this episode, and so he made this list just for Veda.

811
00:32:00.820 --> 00:32:02.420
And I have it from the script.

812
00:32:02.620 --> 00:32:03.620
Oh, fantastic.

813
00:32:03.800 --> 00:32:07.940
Okay, so this is what everyone was intended to give.

814
00:32:08.020 --> 00:32:09.820
And we got a lot of fan questions about this.

815
00:32:09.920 --> 00:32:15.820
Like, a lot of people wrote in and said, you know, eventually Michael's going to get the paintball lessons from Dwight.

816
00:32:15.940 --> 00:32:18.680
But they're like, who did Dwight intend that to go to?

817
00:32:18.840 --> 00:32:20.620
So, I have all the answers right here.

818
00:32:20.680 --> 00:32:21.040
Are you ready?

819
00:32:21.220 --> 00:32:21.480
Yeah.

820
00:32:21.940 --> 00:32:22.280
Okay.

821
00:32:22.800 --> 00:32:26.900
Dwight got Phyllis the paintball lessons and the pellets.

822
00:32:27.240 --> 00:32:28.580
That was his gift to Phyllis.

823
00:32:29.080 --> 00:32:31.280
Phyllis made Michael an oven mitt.

824
00:32:31.960 --> 00:32:34.040
Michael got Ryan an iPod.

825
00:32:34.320 --> 00:32:39.980
Ryan got Toby a book of short stories by George Saunders, who happens to be one of Mike Schur's favorite writers.

826
00:32:40.380 --> 00:32:42.400
Toby got Angela the baby poster.

827
00:32:42.740 --> 00:32:45.020
Angela bought Stanley a picture frame.

828
00:32:45.700 --> 00:32:47.780
Stanley got Kelly a nameplate.

829
00:32:48.300 --> 00:32:50.420
Kelly got Oscar a shower radio.

830
00:32:51.020 --> 00:32:53.400
Oscar got Creed a shamrock key chain.

831
00:32:53.840 --> 00:32:56.460
Creed got Jim one of his own shirts.

832
00:32:57.180 --> 00:32:58.900
Jim got Pam the teapot.

833
00:32:59.040 --> 00:33:00.840
And this is something that got cut out.

834
00:33:01.140 --> 00:33:03.880
Pam made Meredith a drawing of The Office.

835
00:33:03.880 --> 00:33:05.960
I read about that online.

836
00:33:06.360 --> 00:33:06.520
Yeah.

837
00:33:06.660 --> 00:33:07.900
And there was this big thing.

838
00:33:08.100 --> 00:33:09.440
It's in the deleted scenes.

839
00:33:09.680 --> 00:33:11.200
This is something I have to tell you.

840
00:33:11.320 --> 00:33:13.300
I got a DVD player for Christmas.

841
00:33:13.300 --> 00:33:13.940
What?

842
00:33:14.340 --> 00:33:16.400
My husband got me a DVD player.

843
00:33:16.620 --> 00:33:18.220
So I got the CDs.

844
00:33:18.220 --> 00:33:19.800
He bought me the CD set.

845
00:33:20.040 --> 00:33:21.520
And I got a DVD player.

846
00:33:21.660 --> 00:33:24.480
And last night, I got to watch all the deleted scenes.

847
00:33:24.720 --> 00:33:26.940
Oh, Angela, you must be so happy.

848
00:33:26.960 --> 00:33:27.820
I was so happy.

849
00:33:27.820 --> 00:33:28.820
And there's so many.

850
00:33:29.140 --> 00:33:29.580
Oh, yeah.

851
00:33:29.820 --> 00:33:30.280
There's so many.

852
00:33:30.280 --> 00:33:34.280
For the Christmas episode, you guys, there are so many great deleted scenes.

853
00:33:34.460 --> 00:33:36.280
I don't want to get us off topic here.

854
00:33:36.640 --> 00:33:41.300
But there in the deleted scenes, Meredith opens up her painting.

855
00:33:41.660 --> 00:33:42.740
That is from Pam.

856
00:33:42.880 --> 00:33:44.080
And it's a drawing of The Office.

857
00:33:44.660 --> 00:33:47.000
Well, there's a big backstory here.

858
00:33:47.160 --> 00:33:51.100
Again, with Phil, I don't do Pam's drawings.

859
00:33:51.300 --> 00:33:52.500
People ask me that all the time.

860
00:33:52.680 --> 00:33:54.060
I'm not an artiSt.

861
00:33:54.060 --> 00:33:58.720
I mean, we've talked about this, or have we, that I do cartoons.

862
00:33:58.720 --> 00:33:59.820
I do cartooning.

863
00:33:59.960 --> 00:34:01.300
She's very good at cartooning.

864
00:34:01.380 --> 00:34:03.240
And I have a few that you've drawn that I've saved.

865
00:34:03.420 --> 00:34:04.660
I think you're fantastic.

866
00:34:05.040 --> 00:34:07.100
Well, I love my little expressive cartoons.

867
00:34:07.280 --> 00:34:10.860
But I needed Pam and wanted Pam to be a better artist than I am.

868
00:34:11.480 --> 00:34:15.280
So there is a young art student that does all of Pam's drawings.

869
00:34:15.480 --> 00:34:20.340
They went out to a bunch of people, like 12 different artists,

870
00:34:21.880 --> 00:34:26.340
to turn in samples, to be the artist behind Pam.

871
00:34:26.540 --> 00:34:27.860
And they picked a young woman.

872
00:34:28.300 --> 00:34:30.660
Now, Jenna, I read, and you can tell me if this is true.

873
00:34:31.000 --> 00:34:37.400
I read that the first painting that they had for this episode to give to Meredith from Pam,

874
00:34:37.640 --> 00:34:42.940
that they had one of our set art people, who was a man, do it.

875
00:34:43.060 --> 00:34:43.240
Yeah.

876
00:34:43.420 --> 00:34:45.320
And when they looked at it, it looked too masculine.

877
00:34:45.540 --> 00:34:45.780
Yeah.

878
00:34:45.960 --> 00:34:48.100
And so then they went out to female artists.

879
00:34:48.280 --> 00:34:48.740
That's true.

880
00:34:48.940 --> 00:34:50.120
To have a little bit of a softer touch.

881
00:34:50.340 --> 00:34:50.460
Yeah.

882
00:34:50.700 --> 00:34:53.900
And there were something like 12 different artists who all submitted their work.

883
00:34:54.660 --> 00:34:56.020
And I wish I knew her name.

884
00:34:56.140 --> 00:34:57.080
Unfortunately, I don't.

885
00:34:57.180 --> 00:35:00.860
But maybe I can find that out and reveal that in a future episode.

886
00:35:01.240 --> 00:35:02.820
And then so finally, two more gifts.

887
00:35:02.960 --> 00:35:05.680
Meredith got Dwight some shot glasses from Cancun.

888
00:35:05.840 --> 00:35:07.920
And Kevin got himself a foot bath.

889
00:35:08.100 --> 00:35:10.660
Guys, around 5 minutes, 55 seconds,

890
00:35:10.780 --> 00:35:13.700
there is a scene where Michael is talking to Jim at Jim's desk.

891
00:35:13.740 --> 00:35:17.680
This is when he reveals that he got Ryan for Secret Santa.

892
00:35:18.260 --> 00:35:21.700
And I just want to say, you see a ton of background action.

893
00:35:22.180 --> 00:35:23.960
Angela, you're walking from reception.

894
00:35:24.400 --> 00:35:27.200
Over Steve's shoulder, you see Toby and Mindy talking.

895
00:35:27.440 --> 00:35:27.640
Yeah.

896
00:35:28.180 --> 00:35:30.680
They are 100% not in character.

897
00:35:30.920 --> 00:35:32.500
Not in character at all.

898
00:35:32.680 --> 00:35:33.420
I saw that too.

899
00:35:33.420 --> 00:35:36.500
I was like, they're just talking about probably something in the writer's room

900
00:35:36.500 --> 00:35:37.700
or a story pitch.

901
00:35:37.800 --> 00:35:39.040
Or they're just having a conversation.

902
00:35:39.600 --> 00:35:39.740
Yeah.

903
00:35:39.860 --> 00:35:41.680
I mean, Paul is just being Paul.

904
00:35:41.840 --> 00:35:41.960
Yeah.

905
00:35:42.080 --> 00:35:44.820
If anyone's curious, the difference between Toby and Paul,

906
00:35:44.980 --> 00:35:46.440
go to 5 minutes, 55 seconds.

907
00:35:46.720 --> 00:35:48.980
And you can see Paul and Mindy having a conversation in the background.

908
00:35:49.100 --> 00:35:49.220
Yeah.

909
00:35:49.220 --> 00:35:49.760
Yeah, exactly.

910
00:35:51.180 --> 00:35:52.380
Tree lighting.

911
00:35:52.840 --> 00:35:53.240
Okay.

912
00:35:53.240 --> 00:35:54.780
I've been waiting for this moment.

913
00:35:55.220 --> 00:35:56.380
The Christmas tree lighting.

914
00:35:56.840 --> 00:36:01.240
This starts the beginning of Everyone Happy, Angela Pissed.

915
00:36:02.800 --> 00:36:06.880
So this Christmas tree, the top of it has been hacked off by Kevin.

916
00:36:07.060 --> 00:36:10.580
It is covered in so much tinsel.

917
00:36:10.800 --> 00:36:11.040
Yeah.

918
00:36:11.420 --> 00:36:12.460
So much tinsel.

919
00:36:12.820 --> 00:36:15.240
It has a smattering of just blue and red ball ornaments.

920
00:36:15.240 --> 00:36:17.180
It's just not their best effort.

921
00:36:17.460 --> 00:36:22.380
And then it has the tiniest of tiny white lights, thanks to Phyllis.

922
00:36:22.540 --> 00:36:24.160
So Dwight makes a big deal of it.

923
00:36:24.340 --> 00:36:28.060
He takes the outlet, like the plug.

924
00:36:28.180 --> 00:36:28.820
What do you call it?

925
00:36:29.440 --> 00:36:30.040
The plug?

926
00:36:30.140 --> 00:36:30.660
The plug.

927
00:36:30.820 --> 00:36:32.340
He takes the plug from Stanley.

928
00:36:32.340 --> 00:36:33.360
He wants to plug it in.

929
00:36:33.420 --> 00:36:34.600
He's like, just like Rockefeller Center.

930
00:36:34.900 --> 00:36:36.460
And everyone gathers around.

931
00:36:36.460 --> 00:36:40.540
And it's like, and Phyllis is like, I'm sorry.

932
00:36:40.540 --> 00:36:46.620
And at 6 minutes, 38 seconds, you see my first pissed off face.

933
00:36:47.100 --> 00:36:48.300
Dang it, Phyllis.

934
00:36:48.500 --> 00:36:52.100
It's also one of those moments where I feel like Angela's like, I knew it.

935
00:36:52.260 --> 00:36:52.760
I knew it.

936
00:36:52.760 --> 00:36:55.200
I knew I couldn't trust her to do these lights.

937
00:36:55.400 --> 00:36:57.460
Why do I even have her do anything?

938
00:36:57.460 --> 00:36:57.680
Ever.

939
00:36:57.680 --> 00:36:58.960
Why do you have anyone do anything?

940
00:36:59.040 --> 00:36:59.300
Yeah.

941
00:36:59.820 --> 00:37:01.820
You can't let anyone do anything.

942
00:37:02.000 --> 00:37:02.960
These people are worthless.

943
00:37:03.240 --> 00:37:03.600
Exactly.

944
00:37:04.260 --> 00:37:08.940
You know, that Christmas tree light thing is based on a real thing from Mike Schur's life.

945
00:37:08.940 --> 00:37:09.920
I know.

946
00:37:11.300 --> 00:37:16.000
He said that when he and his wife got their first tree in New York, he bought a bunch of

947
00:37:16.000 --> 00:37:18.460
small lights for the tree and he wrapped them around.

948
00:37:18.600 --> 00:37:20.460
And when he plugged it in, you couldn't really see them.

949
00:37:22.220 --> 00:37:23.200
I love that.

950
00:37:23.200 --> 00:37:27.000
I love when writers work those little moments from their real life into the show.

951
00:37:27.260 --> 00:37:31.300
I thought, speaking about people who are acting like themselves instead of their characters,

952
00:37:31.540 --> 00:37:35.100
I thought Jim's talking head about Creed's gift is so John.

953
00:37:35.380 --> 00:37:36.120
It is John.

954
00:37:36.340 --> 00:37:37.800
That is John right there.

955
00:37:37.940 --> 00:37:38.100
Yeah.

956
00:37:38.100 --> 00:37:41.820
All the delivery, the smile, all of it.

957
00:37:41.980 --> 00:37:44.800
And then, of course, Creed's talking head made me laugh so hard.

958
00:37:45.040 --> 00:37:47.120
Creed is very funny in this episode.

959
00:37:47.300 --> 00:37:52.340
I mean, everybody has some great moments, but Creed cracked me up a bunch in this episode.

960
00:37:52.500 --> 00:37:54.260
So now Secret Santa is starting.

961
00:37:54.520 --> 00:37:54.700
Yep.

962
00:37:55.180 --> 00:37:57.720
Everyone is gathered around in some office chairs.

963
00:37:57.720 --> 00:38:03.660
And I want to say, truly, I know we were joking about Charles McDougal, but the amount of energy

964
00:38:03.660 --> 00:38:10.560
and movement that he uses the camera to give this scene of people sitting in a circle, I

965
00:38:10.560 --> 00:38:13.060
mean, it is impressive from a directorial standpoint.

966
00:38:13.060 --> 00:38:18.040
I think, like, I don't want to be crazy, but I think, like,

967
00:38:18.460 --> 00:38:27.620
film students should study this portion of the episode because I'm imagining myself trying to film a group of people sitting in a circle doing a gift exchange,

968
00:38:27.620 --> 00:38:29.600
and it would not look nearly this dynamic.

969
00:38:29.600 --> 00:38:31.360
It's really, really impressive directing.

970
00:38:31.640 --> 00:38:32.580
No, he's great.

971
00:38:32.700 --> 00:38:33.620
He is really great.

972
00:38:33.860 --> 00:38:37.600
Okay, so we're starting the Secret Santa, and Pam opens Jim's teapot.

973
00:38:37.780 --> 00:38:44.140
She loves it, but Dwight moves things along so quickly that she doesn't have time to look inside or notice the card that's in the box.

974
00:38:44.140 --> 00:38:46.120
Dwight wants no chitty chat between gifts.

975
00:38:46.220 --> 00:38:47.020
He's like, go, go, go, go, go.

976
00:38:47.120 --> 00:38:48.420
He's me coming in today.

977
00:38:48.580 --> 00:38:49.020
He is.

978
00:38:49.040 --> 00:38:50.500
He's like, save it for the mic.

979
00:38:51.120 --> 00:38:52.580
So he's moving things along.

980
00:38:52.580 --> 00:38:53.280
So it's Pam.

981
00:38:53.520 --> 00:38:54.600
And then the next one.

982
00:38:54.700 --> 00:39:01.320
We find out that Michael buys Ryan a video iPod that costs $400.

983
00:39:02.000 --> 00:39:03.960
You guys, this was not product placement.

984
00:39:04.200 --> 00:39:04.800
It was not.

985
00:39:04.960 --> 00:39:06.600
So many people wanted to know.

986
00:39:06.760 --> 00:39:08.460
Yeah, we were not paid.

987
00:39:08.460 --> 00:39:11.640
It was just sort of a really cool topical gift at the time.

988
00:39:11.780 --> 00:39:11.960
Yeah.

989
00:39:11.960 --> 00:39:19.140
And they were trying to think of a gift that would sort of be a showstopper that Michael would think was very impressive that everyone would want.

990
00:39:19.540 --> 00:39:20.720
So this was coincidence.

991
00:39:20.720 --> 00:39:22.060
We weren't paid to use it.

992
00:39:22.200 --> 00:39:23.200
So I read that.

993
00:39:24.320 --> 00:39:25.380
Well, here's something.

994
00:39:25.660 --> 00:39:28.700
A ton of people wanted to know who kept it at the end.

995
00:39:28.820 --> 00:39:29.100
Nobody.

996
00:39:29.340 --> 00:39:30.980
We weren't allowed to keep any of the stuff.

997
00:39:30.980 --> 00:39:40.020
It all goes into a giant warehouse and it gets labeled for the episode for props because if for some reason we have to go back and reshoot something,

998
00:39:40.220 --> 00:39:42.120
they take it off the shelf and they bring it back in.

999
00:39:42.280 --> 00:39:42.780
That's true.

1000
00:39:42.900 --> 00:39:47.640
I don't know what happens after it's been in the warehouse for a while, but it just goes to prop house storage.

1001
00:39:48.080 --> 00:39:51.620
I feel like it's still in a box labeled the office Christmas party.

1002
00:39:51.780 --> 00:39:52.620
It probably is.

1003
00:39:52.620 --> 00:39:55.100
There was a fan question from Beard Up, Beard Down.

1004
00:39:55.320 --> 00:39:57.020
Was the iPod sponsored by Apple?

1005
00:39:57.160 --> 00:39:57.860
It wasn't.

1006
00:39:57.960 --> 00:39:59.020
We said it was not.

1007
00:39:59.220 --> 00:40:00.420
It's just a total coincidence.

1008
00:40:00.680 --> 00:40:02.320
But there's more coincidence.

1009
00:40:03.480 --> 00:40:12.720
So the week after this episode aired, Apple revealed that you could now download episodes of The Office onto these video iPods.

1010
00:40:12.920 --> 00:40:14.840
Again, this was not planned.

1011
00:40:15.160 --> 00:40:20.740
And then The Office became the number one downloaded show on iTunes.

1012
00:40:21.080 --> 00:40:21.600
Yes.

1013
00:40:21.900 --> 00:40:23.500
The number one downloaded show.

1014
00:40:23.740 --> 00:40:27.860
I remember Rainn Wilson turned to me and said, I think we're going to make it.

1015
00:40:27.860 --> 00:40:34.000
But I think we're going to – this was the first moment it felt like the tide was turning for us and that we might not get canceled.

1016
00:40:34.300 --> 00:40:34.680
All right.

1017
00:40:34.780 --> 00:40:40.840
So next up, Michael gets his gift, the oven mitt knitted by Phyllis.

1018
00:40:41.080 --> 00:40:41.400
Oof.

1019
00:40:41.880 --> 00:40:44.220
Now, everyone had a $20 limit, you guys.

1020
00:40:44.360 --> 00:40:48.320
That's why this iPod really shakes everything up because he spent $400.

1021
00:40:48.740 --> 00:40:49.080
Yes.

1022
00:40:49.320 --> 00:40:49.680
Yes.

1023
00:40:50.360 --> 00:40:56.060
And he has his line where he says, I only – he says, out in the hallway, he's holding the mitt.

1024
00:40:56.140 --> 00:40:57.600
And he says, do you know what this says?

